WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.712
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:08.235
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.535 --> 00:00:15.309
Unit twenty-three: Health Systems. In this unit, you will discuss healthcare and speculate about the past.

4
00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:17.190
healthcare.

5
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.749
healthcare means medical services provided to people.

6
00:00:21.049 --> 00:00:23.548
Good healthcare should be available to everyone.

7
00:00:24.248 --> 00:00:26.865
Your turn. Say: healthcare.

8
00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:30.543
healthcare.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.737
public hospital.

10
00:00:33.437 --> 00:00:35.924
public hospital means a hospital run by the government.

11
00:00:36.224 --> 00:00:38.433
Treatment at the public hospital is cheaper.

12
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.692
Your turn. Say: public hospital.

13
00:00:44.392 --> 00:00:45.683
public hospital.

14
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:47.684
private clinic.

15
00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:52.102
private clinic means a clinic run by a company, where patients pay more.

16
00:00:52.402 --> 00:00:54.994
She went to a private clinic for faster treatment.

17
00:00:55.694 --> 00:00:58.497
Your turn. Say: private clinic.

18
00:01:01.197 --> 00:01:02.372
private clinic.

19
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:04.872
health insurance plan.

20
00:01:05.572 --> 00:01:09.371
health insurance plan means an arrangement that pays your medical costs.

21
00:01:09.671 --> 00:01:11.984
Our company offers a health insurance plan.

22
00:01:12.684 --> 00:01:15.743
Your turn. Say: health insurance plan.

23
00:01:18.443 --> 00:01:20.024
health insurance plan.

24
00:01:21.017 --> 00:01:21.925
epidemic.

25
00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:25.913
epidemic means a disease that spreads quickly in one area.

26
00:01:26.213 --> 00:01:28.956
There was a dengue epidemic last year.

27
00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.844
Your turn. Say: epidemic.

28
00:01:34.544 --> 00:01:35.556
epidemic.

29
00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:37.435
pandemic.

30
00:01:38.135 --> 00:01:42.120
pandemic means a disease that spreads across many countries.

31
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.327
The pandemic changed how we work.

32
00:01:45.027 --> 00:01:47.261
Your turn. Say: pandemic.

33
00:01:49.961 --> 00:01:50.974
pandemic.

34
00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:53.112
vaccination.

35
00:01:53.812 --> 00:01:57.356
vaccination means giving a vaccine to protect against disease.

36
00:01:57.656 --> 00:02:00.097
Vaccination saved millions of lives.

37
00:02:00.797 --> 00:02:03.182
Your turn. Say: vaccination.

38
00:02:05.882 --> 00:02:06.895
vaccination.

39
00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:08.873
outbreak.

40
00:02:09.573 --> 00:02:12.176
outbreak means the sudden start of a disease.

41
00:02:12.476 --> 00:02:14.627
Health workers stopped the outbreak quickly.

42
00:02:15.327 --> 00:02:17.677
Your turn. Say: outbreak.

43
00:02:20.377 --> 00:02:21.378
outbreak.

44
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:24.476
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:24.776 --> 00:02:27.170
Did you hear about the outbreak in the next province?

46
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:33.191
Yes. It must have started in the rainy season, because of mosquitoes.

47
00:02:34.483 --> 00:02:37.563
The village clinic can't have been ready for so many patients.

48
00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.802
They might have sent people to the public hospital in the city.

49
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:46.266
Luckily, the vaccination campaign has started now.

50
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.330
Good. It could have become an epidemic without it.

51
00:02:51.617 --> 00:02:54.173
Grammar focus: Speculating about the past.

52
00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:58.110
Use must have, might have and can't have to speculate about the past.

53
00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:03.718
Must have means you're sure; might have means it's possible; can't have means you're sure it didn't happen.

54
00:03:04.018 --> 00:03:06.866
For example: It must have spread through mosquitoes.

55
00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:11.650
Could have can also mean something was possible but didn't happen: It could have been worse.

56
00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.558
Now read and listen. Lessons from the Pandemic.

57
00:03:15.858 --> 00:03:19.959
The pandemic showed how important strong healthcare systems are.

58
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.061
Countries with good public hospitals must have saved many lives.

59
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.451
In some places, private clinics could have helped more if they had worked together.

60
00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.549
Vaccination campaigns were the key to stopping new outbreaks.

61
00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:40.498
Experts say that preparing for the next epidemic must start now.

62
00:03:41.783 --> 00:03:44.192
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:44.492 --> 00:03:47.710
A disease that spreads across many countries is a blank.

64
00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.408
A, pandemic. B, epidemic. C, outbreak.

65
00:03:55.417 --> 00:03:57.730
The answer is A: pandemic.

66
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:02.148
The streets are wet. It blank rained last night.

67
00:04:02.448 --> 00:04:06.310
A, must have. B, can't have. C, should have.

68
00:04:10.317 --> 00:04:12.351
The answer is A: must have.

69
00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.293
She blank seen you. She was in Japan.

70
00:04:16.593 --> 00:04:20.479
A, must have. B, can't have. C, might have.

71
00:04:24.483 --> 00:04:26.135
The answer is B: can't have.

72
00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.963
A hospital run by the government is a blank.

73
00:04:30.263 --> 00:04:35.356
A, private clinic. B, public hospital. C, health insurance plan.

74
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.640
The answer is B: public hospital.

75
00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:46.566
According to the text, what was the key to stopping outbreaks?

76
00:04:46.866 --> 00:04:51.657
A, private clinics. B, vaccination campaigns. C, new hospitals.

77
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.079
The answer is B: vaccination campaigns.

78
00:04:59.583 --> 00:05:03.745
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you think helped your country most during the pandemic?

79
00:05:09.045 --> 00:05:14.844
Vaccination must have helped the most. Without it, many more people could have become seriously ill.

80
00:05:15.144 --> 00:05:16.783
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:21.933
Great work today! You learned eight new words and speculating about the past.

82
00:05:22.233 --> 00:05:25.420
Today's value is healthy body. Move your body every day.

83
00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.221
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

84
00:05:28.521 --> 00:05:31.162
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

